            Tub size flips the result. Vitacost listed the 2 lb (907 g) Levels tub at $57.99 on the same day. At the 28 servings per tub given in the Amazon listing our <a href='/levels-protein-powder-review/'>Levels review</a> cites, that is about $2.16 per 25 g, more than Isopure's 3 lb tub. Per container, the 5 lb Levels tub holds about 1,704 g of protein and the 3 lb Isopure tub about 1,100 g, so Levels also suits buyers who want fewer reorders.
          </p>

          <p>
            Store matters too. Levels sells mainly through its own Amazon storefront, and our <a href='/levels-vs-ascent-protein/'>Levels vs Ascent comparison</a> recorded Amazon prices well below Vitacost's for the same tubs. To compare any listing yourself, divide the price by the number of servings, divide by the grams of protein per serving, and multiply by 25. Our <a href='/best-whey-protein-isolate/'>best whey protein isolate</a> ranking shows where Isopure's price sits among isolates.
          </p>
